@@ -101,6 +102,26 @@ not depend on, so those registries need a `docker login` first.
 `TAG` may itself carry a digest, as in `--image-tag v0.0.0@sha256:...`. A tag
 that already names a manifest is used as written, and is not looked up.
 
+### Image maps
+
+`--image-map FILE` (or `ATE_IMAGE_MAP`) takes an absolute path to a file with
+one `<image> <reference>` line per image; blank lines and `#` comments are
+ignored. The image is a component's image name (`atelet`, `ateapi`, ...) or
+`envoy-dataplane`; the reference is a `nix:0/nix/store/<hash>-<name>.tar` store
+reference or a reference pinned by digest. Each reference replaces the
+component's `ko://` reference as written: nothing is looked up, and a `nix:0`
+reference is resolved by nix-snapshotter for Kubernetes pods and workers.
+Demo actor images instead use `nix:/nix/store/<hash>-<name>` root trees.
+The installer rejects a Nix reference with the wrong runtime for a component. A component the manifests use but the map lacks fails the install.
+
+The image may instead be an exact reference pinned by digest that a manifest
+names, such as the bundled PostgreSQL's
+`postgres:18-alpine@sha256:<digest> nix:0/nix/store/<hash>-nix-image-postgres.tar`.
+Every occurrence of that reference as a whole token, in the system manifests
+and the PostgreSQL manifest, is replaced; a differently written reference to
+the same image (`docker.io/library/postgres:...`) is not. A reference the map
+does not name is installed as the manifest pins it.
+
 ## Deploy
 
 - `deploy ate-system`
